<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (GPT-5.6 Sol)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol";
    dc:identifier "gpt-5.6-sol-medium".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-21--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch04-21: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.50";
    dc:description "Specific mathematical readings can be analyzed using proofs and simulations, and counterexamples can separate sensitivity from chaotic mixing. The categorical conclusion depends on a contested definition of randomness production, so the claim as stated is not fully resolvable.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/mixed";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Formalize production of randomness as growth in algorithmic or stochastic information conditional on the exact initial state, then compare maps with positive sensitivity but differing information generation. Exact deterministic dynamics can be proved not to create algorithmic information beyond the rule and initial state, while practical entropy notions yield different answers.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Deterministic, finite-precision, and stochastic notions give different verdicts.", "Sensitive dependence and entropy production are related but not identical.", "Ultimate production of randomness is a philosophical rather than standard measurable quantity.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.77"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.501"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-21--gpt--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of wolfram2002-ch04-21 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 0.58";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
